and 1 warning, which I didn't look into.\n\n**What changed**\n- **`DocService/sources/converterservice.js`:** the sync wait loop now starts at 50 ms and doubles each time, up to 1000 ms. It adds up the time it actually waited, and the timeout check (`waitTime > getConvertionTimeout`) works exactly as before.\n- **`tests/unit/converterService.tests.js`:** only the `sleeps` expectations and the matching test title and comment changed. They are now `[50]` twice, `[50,100,200]`, and `[50,100,200,400,800,1000,1000]` for the timeout case.\n- **The code change had to be redone.** The diff described in the earlier Executor log was not on the branch, so I applied it again.\n\n**Measurement** (native stack, JWT on, sync docx→odt, 10 runs one after another)\n\n| Server | p50 | mean |\n|---|---|---|\n| Installed server on :80 | 1013 ms | 1014 ms |\n| Worktree DocService from source on :8099, old code | 1018 ms | 1018 ms |\n| Same, with this change | 166 ms | 169 ms |\n\nThat saves about 850 ms per sync request. The two source runs used the same database, RabbitMQ and converters as the installed server, so the before/after comparison is like for like.\n\n**Decisions and surprises**\n- **The perf oracle doesn't work on this stack.** `.theseus/oracle/perf/e2e-convert.js` returns error -8 on every pair: it sends no JWT and expects the Docker setup on :8080. I measured with a scratch copy that signs requests with the server's secret instead. That copy is not committed, because the oracle script is outside my target files.\n- **Follow-up requested:** a packet to fix that script for the native stack, recorded in `.theseus/spawn/` and committed with the work. It declares `requires: [documentserver]`.\n- **Stash slip:** I briefly stashed my own change by mistake. I restored it by its SHA and dropped only my own entry. The final diff is correct.\n- The Executor log, Lessons for the Atlas and the friction line are filled in.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas**\n- In sync mode, the fixed 1-second poll was where most of the time went.\n- To measure a DocService change on the native stack, run `DocService/sources/server.js` with `NODE_CONFIG_DIR=/etc/euro-office/documentserver` and a `NODE_CONFIG` port override, and sign requests with the inbox secret.","ttft_ms":2285,"type":"result","duration_ms":135496,"uuid":"820d5566-d2f8-4b20-a7d8-71e40fd2b631","ttft_stream_ms":1194,"time_to_request_ms":363,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":212,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":24,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":13,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":13,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":13,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":9,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":26,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":9,"request_build":15},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":96,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":163,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":213,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":228,"process_anon_mib_result":137,"process_peak_rss_mib":251,"process_cpu_ms_turn":3444,"process_wall_ms_turn":135496,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1342,"process_wall_ms_streaming":70475,"main_stream_count":21,"main_stream_event_count":1339,"main_stream_chunk_count":794,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":10,"cpu_ms":20,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":10,"ambient_wait_ms":10,"render_ms":2,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":1194,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":20993409,"warm_spare_claimed":false,"flag_fetch_kick":"started_in_init_warm","time_origin_ms":1793656449914.646,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"process_start_tuning":0}
